  "notes": "The writer-forward, roots-leaning female pole of 2000s–2010s radio. The entry credits her with \"the widest dynamic range of any artist here — several singles run on brushes, floor tom and shaker only, while the rockers use a hard quarter-kick backbeat with overdriven room mics,\" so the velocity tiers span further than any other model in this batch and the perc lanes carry brush-and-tom textures rather than a hat wash. Minor-tonic singles are documented, not inferred: \"F♯ minor and E minor appear on hits,\" which is the minor key weighting and the i–VII–VI family. The bass is \"sparse; drop-out verses are common, with the bass entering at the chorus,\" and the entry adds \"no programmed sub on the core catalogue\" — so no `bass808` block is authored here at all. Melody is \"mid-alto, conversational, with a narrow verse range and a chorus that leaps a sixth; ornament is a country cry/break rather than melisma,\" which is a step-heavy interval mix with a real leap share and an octave-jump probability near the floor. The arrangement device is named as the section's most-used: \"strip to voice and one instrument before the last chorus.\" ⚠ Boundary flag: the honky-tonk cuts push toward shuffle and those grooves belong to `country-shuffle`. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: high-medium); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF] and songdata's 155–190 figures fold onto the stated band. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
